  "semantics": [
    "Input strides are rows*columns,columns,1 using wrapped uint32 arithmetic. Operation bytes1/2 select cached row and column strides. Byte0 and batch are unused. Output rows and columns are cached and loop bounds are signed.",
    "Data moves as raw32-bit words: signaling NaNs, payloads, subnormals and signed zero retain bits with unchanged FPSCR. Copies are forward and reads observe prior writes under overlap. Input/output descriptor and operation fields can be overwritten only after cached fields are read.",
    "Real C constructor emits a normal C function relocation; C probe invokes callback via indirect branch. Source replay has no stock mapping or algorithm boundary model. Actual callback identity is checked before measurement-only normalization of the pointer word."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Selectors1/2 must be0..2. Native out-of-table stack indexing is outside the contract, not assigned a new fallback behavior. Invalid pointers, huge physical buffer spans and concurrent mutation remain unproven.",
    "Public RAM/full FPSCR, saved R4-R11/S16-S31, SP, masks and R0 are checked.8192 private stack bytes below incoming SP and caller-clobbered scratch/APSR are outside proof.",
    "All92 body bytes execute, but this is not exhaustive input/interleaving proof. FPU activation is primed; cold activation and timing are untested.",
    "Nine callback bindings and five parent SpO2 stages remain unresolved.923-unit relocatable composition has76 application and22 boot imports; final startup, physical sensors and complete boot remain unverified."
  ],
